The attached image is a Western blot depicting the presence of pro-IL-1β in cell lysates and its active, cleaved form in the supernatant of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells following various treatments. The blot shows that pro-IL-1β (~30kD) is present in cell lysates, particularly when stimulated with LPS and Nano-11. More importantly, the active IL-1β (~15kD, referred to as 17kD in the PDF text) is observed in the supernatant, notably at high levels after stimulation with Nano-11, and even more so when Nano-11 is combined with LPS. This confirms that Nano-11 induces the cleavage and secretion of biologically active IL-1β, a crucial pro-inflammatory cytokine for dendritic cell activation, as reported in Figure 7C of the PDF.